      "text": "Consider a demand paging system with three frames, and the following page reference string: 1 2 3 4 5 4 1 6 4 5 1 3 2. The contents of the frames are as follows initially and after each reference (from left to right): | initially | after\n| - | $1^{*}$ | $2^{*}$ | $3^{*}$ | $4^{*}$ | $5^{*}$ | 4 | 1 | $6^{*}$ | 4 | 5 | $1^{*}$ | $3^{*}$ | $2^{*}$\n| - | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 2\n| - | - | 2 | 2 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 1 | 1\n| - | - | - | 3 | 3 | 5 | 5 | 5 | 5 | 5 | 5 | 5 | 3 | 3 The \\*-marked references cause page replacements. Which one or more of the following could be the page replacement policy/policies in use?",
