    {
      "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-5-24-5",
      "topic": "synchronization",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "nat",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 1991,
      "text": "Consider the following scheme for implementing a critical section in a situation with three processes $P_{i}, P_{j}$ and $P_{k}$. a. Does the scheme ensure mutual exclusion in the critical section? Briefly explain.",
      "options": [],
      "code_blocks": [
        {
          "lang": "txt",
          "code": "Pi;\nrepeat\n    flag[i] := true;\n    while flag [j] or flag[k] do\n        case turn of\n        j: if flag [j] then\n        begin\n            flag [i] := false;\n            while turn != i do skip;\n            flag [i] := true;\n        end;\n        k: if flag [k] then\n        begin\n            flag [i] := false,\n            while turn != i do skip;\n            flag [i] := true\n        end\n    end\n    critical section\n    if turn = i then turn := j;\n        flag [i] := false\n    non-critical section\nuntil false;"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume3.pdf",
        "volume": "filter1_volume3",
        "ref": "5.24.5",
