    {
      "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-5-24-24",
      "topic": "synchronization",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2003,
      "text": "Suppose we want to synchronize two concurrent processes P and Q using binary semaphores S and T. The code for the processes P and Q is shown below. | Process P: | Process Q:\n| while(1){W:print &#x27;0&#x27;;print &#x27;0&#x27;;X:} | while(1){Y:print &#x27;1&#x27;;print &#x27;1&#x27;;Z:} Synchronization statements can be inserted only at points $W, X, Y$, and $Z$ Which of the following will always lead to an output staring with '001100110011'?",
      "options": [
        "$P(S)$ at $W, V(S)$ at $X, P(T)$ at $Y, V(T)$ at $Z, S$ and $T$ initially 1",
        "$P(S)$ at $W, V(T)$ at $X, P(T)$ at $Y, V(S)$ at $Z, S$ initially 1, and $T$ initially 0",
        "$P(S)$ at $W, V(T)$ at $X, P(T)$ at $Y, V(S)$ at $Z, S$ and $T$ initially 1",
        "$P(S)$ at $W, V(S)$ at $X, P(T)$ at $Y, V(T)$ at $Z, S$ initially 1, and $T$ initially 0"
      ],
      "answer": [
        1
      ],
      "origin": {
