      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2003,
      "text": "Suppose we want to synchronize two concurrent processes P and Q using binary semaphores S and T. The code for the processes P and Q is shown below. | Process P: | Process Q:\n| while(1) {W:print ‘0’;print ‘0’;X:} | while(1) {Y:print ‘1’;print ‘1’;Z:} Synchronization statements can be inserted only at points W, X, Y, and Z Which of the following will ensure that the output string never contains a substring of the form $01^{n}0$ and $10^{n}1$ where $n$ is odd?",
      "options": [
        "$P(S)$ at $W, V(S)$ at $X, P(T)$ at $Y, V(T)$ at $Z, S$ and $T$ initially 1",
