    {
      "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-5-24-26",
      "topic": "synchronization",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2004,
      "text": "Consider two processes $P_{1}$ and $P_{2}$ accessing the shared variables X and Y protected by two binary semaphores $S_{X}$ and $S_{Y}$ respectively, both initialized to 1. P and V denote the usual semaphore operators, where P decrements the semaphore value, and V increments the semaphore value. The pseudo-code of $P_{1}$ and $P_{2}$ is as follows: | $P_1$: | $P_2$:\n| While true do { | While true do {\n| $L_1: \\dots \\dots$ | $L_3: \\dots \\dots$\n| $L_2: \\dots \\dots$ | $L_4: \\dots \\dots$\n| $\\mathrm{X} = \\mathrm{X} + 1$; | $\\mathrm{Y} = \\mathrm{Y} + 1$;\n| $Y = Y - 1$; | $X = Y - 1$;\n| $V(S_X)$; | $V(S_Y)$;\n| $V(S_Y)$; | $V(S_X)$;\n| } | } In order to avoid deadlock, the correct operators at $L_{1}$, $L_{2}$, $L_{3}$ and $L_{4}$ are respectively.",
      "options": [
        "$P(S_{Y}), P(S_{X}); P(S_{X}), P(S_{Y})$",
        "$P(S_X), P(S_Y); P(S_Y), P(S_X)$",
        "$P(S_X), P(S_X); P(S_Y), P(S_Y)$",
        "$P(S_X), P(S_Y); P(S_X), P(S_Y)$"
      ],
      "answer": [
        3
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume3.pdf",
        "volume": "filter1_volume3",
        "ref": "5.24.26",
        "exam": "GATE CSE 2004 | Question: 48",
