    {
      "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-5-24-31",
      "topic": "synchronization",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2009,
      "text": "The enter\\_CS() and leave\\_CS() functions to implement critical section of a process are realized using test-and-set instruction as follows: In the above solution, $X$ is a memory location associated with the $CS$ and is initialized to 0. Now consider the following statements: I. The above solution to CS problem is deadlock-free II. The solution is starvation free III. The processes enter CS in FIFO order IV. More than one process can enter CS at the same time Which of the above statements are TRUE?",
      "options": [
        "(I) only",
        "(I) and (II)",
        "(II) and (III)",
        "(IV) only"
      ],
      "answer": [
        0
      ],
      "code_blocks": [
        {
          "lang": "txt",
          "code": "void enter_CS(X)\n{\n    while(test-and-set(X));\n}\n\nvoid leave_CS(X)\n{\n    X = 0;\n}"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
