    {
      "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-5-24-40",
      "topic": "synchronization",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "year": 2016,
      "text": "Consider the following proposed solution for the critical section problem. There are n processes: $P_{0}\\ldots P_{n-1}$. In the code, function pmax returns an integer not smaller than any of its arguments. For all i, $t[i]$ is initialized to zero. Code for $P_{i}$; Which of the following is TRUE about the above solution?",
      "options": [
        "At most one process can be in the critical section at any time",
        "The bounded wait condition is satisfied",
        "The progress condition is satisfied",
        "It cannot cause a deadlock"
      ],
      "answer": [
        0
      ],
      "code_blocks": [
        {
          "lang": "javascript",
          "code": "do {\n    c[i]=1; t[i]= pmax (t[0],...,t[n-1])+1; c[i]=0;\n    for every j != i in {0,...,n-1} {\n        while (c[j]);\n        while (t[j] != 0 && t[j] <=t[i]);\n    }\n    Critical Section;\n    t[i]=0;\n\n    Remainder Section;\n\n} while (true);"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume3.pdf",
        "volume": "filter1_volume3",
        "ref": "5.24.40",
        "exam": "GATE CSE 2016 | Set 1 | Question: 50",
        "section": "Process Synchronization",
        "paper_question": "50",
        "tags": [
          "gatecse-2016-set1",
          "operating-system",
          "process-synchronization",
          "difficult",
          "ambiguous"
        ],
        "topic_source": "section"
      }
    },
    {
