      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2016,
      "text": "Consider the following two-process synchronization solution. | PROCESS 0 | Process 1\n| Entry: loop while (turn == 1); (critical section) | Entry: loop while (turn == 0); (critical section)\n| Exit: turn = 1; | Exit turn = 0; The shared variable turn is initialized to zero. Which one of the following is TRUE?",
      "options": [
        "This is a correct two- process synchronization solution.",
        "This solution violates mutual exclusion requirement.",
        "This solution violates progress requirement.",
        "This solution violates bounded wait requirement."
