      "text": "Consider three concurrent processes $P_{1}, P_{2}$ and $P_{3}$ as shown below, which access a shared variable D that has been initialized to 100. | $P_{1}$ | $P_{2}$ | $P_{3}$\n| $\\vdots$ | $\\vdots$ | $\\vdots$\n| $\\vdots$ | $\\vdots$ | $\\vdots$\n| $D = D + 20$ | $D = D - 50$ | $D = D + 10$\n| $\\vdots$ | $\\vdots$ | $\\vdots$\n| $\\vdots$ | $\\vdots$ | $\\vdots$ The processes are executed on a uniprocessor system running a time-shared operating system. If the minimum and maximum possible values of $D$ after the three processes have completed execution are $X$ and $Y$ respectively, then the value of $Y - X$ is \\_\\_\\_\\_",
