      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2024,
      "text": "Consider a multi-threaded program with two threads T1 and T2. The threads share two semaphores: s1 (initialized to 1) and s2 (initialized to 0). The threads also share a global variable x (initialized to 0). The threads execute the code shown below. Which of the following outcomes is/are possible when threads T1 and T2 execute concurrently?",
      "options": [
        "T1 runs first and prints 1, T2 runs next and prints 2",
        "T2 runs first and prints 1, T1 runs next and prints 2",
        "T1 runs first and prints 1, T2 does not print anything (deadlock)",
        "T2 runs first and prints 1, T1 does not print anything (deadlock)"
      ],
      "answer": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "code_blocks": [
        {
          "lang": "txt",
          "code": "//code of T 1\nwait (s1);\nx = x+1;\nprint (x);\nwait (s2);\nsignal(s1);"
