      "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-5-25-12",
      "topic": "deadlock",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2005,
      "text": "Suppose n processes, $P_{1}, \\ldots, P_{n}$ share m identical resource units, which can be reserved and released one at a time. The maximum resource requirement of process $P_{i}$ is $s_{i}$, where $s_{i} > 0$. Which one of the following is a sufficient condition for ensuring that deadlock does not occur?",
      "options": [
        "$\\forall i, s_i, < m$",
        "$\\forall i, s_i < n$",
        "$\\sum_{i=1}^{n} s_i < (m+n)$",
        "$\\sum_{i=1}^{n} s_i < (m \\times n)$"
      ],
      "answer": [
        2
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume3.pdf",
