      "year": 2005,
      "text": "Two shared resources $R_{1}$ and $R_{2}$ are used by processes $P_{1}$ and $P_{2}$. Each process has a certain priority for accessing each resource. Let $T_{ij}$ denote the priority of $P_{i}$ for accessing $R_{j}$. A process $P_{i}$ can snatch a resource $R_{k}$ from process $P_{j}$ if $T_{ik}$ is greater than $T_{jk}$. Given the following: 1. $T_{11} > T_{21}$ II. $T_{12} > T_{22}$ III. $T_{11} < T_{21}$ IV. $T_{12} < T_{22}$ Which of the following conditions ensures that $P_{1}$ and $P_{2}$ can never deadlock?",
