      "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-5-28-4",
      "topic": "synchronization",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2008,
      "text": "The P and V operations on counting semaphores, where s is a counting semaphore, are defined as follows: P (s): $\\begin{array}{l} s = s - 1; \\\\ \\text {If} s < 0 \\text {then wait;} \\end{array} V (s)$: $\\begin{array}{l} s = s + 1; \\\\ \\text {If} s \\leq 0 \\text {then wake up process waiting on} s; \\end{array}$ Assume that $P_{b}$ and $V_{b}$ the wait and signal operations on binary semaphores are provided. Two binary semaphores $x_{b}$ and $y_{b}$ are used to implement the semaphore operations $P(s)$ and $V(s)$ as follows: P (s): $\\begin{array}{l} P _ {b} (x _ {b}); \\\\ s = s - 1; \\\\ \\text {if} (s < 0) \\\\ \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{c} V _ {b} (x _ {b}); \\\\ P _ {b} (y _ {b}); \\end{array} \\right. \\\\ \\left. \\begin{array}{l} \\} \\\\ \\text {else} V _ {b} (x _ {b}); \\end{array} \\right. \\end{array} V (s)$: $\\quad \\begin{array}{l} P _ {b} (x _ {b}); \\\\ s = s + 1; \\\\ \\text {if} (s \\leq 0) V _ {b} (y _ {b}); \\\\ V _ {b} (x _ {b}); \\end{array}$ The initial values of $x_{b}$ and $y_{b}$ are respectively",
      "options": [
        "0 and 0",
        "0 and 1",
        "1 and 0",
        "1 and 1"
      ],
      "answer": [
        2
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume3.pdf",
        "volume": "filter1_volume3",
        "ref": "5.28.4",
        "exam": "GATE CSE 2008 | Question: 63",
