    {
      "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-5-28-11",
      "topic": "synchronization",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2006,
      "text": "The wait and signal operations of a monitor are implemented using semaphores as follows. In the following, - $x$ is a condition variable, - mutex is a semaphore initialized to 1, - $x$ \\_sem is a semaphore initialized to 0, - $x$ count is the number of processes waiting on semaphore $x$ sem, initially 0, - next is a semaphore initialized to 0, - next\\_count is the number of processes waiting on semaphore next, initially 0. The body of each procedure that is visible outside the monitor is replaced with the following: Each occurrence of x.wait is replaced with the following: Each occurrence of x.signal is replaced with the following: For correct implementation of the monitor, statements E1 and E2 are, respectively,",
      "options": [
        "$P(x\\_sem), V(next)$ C. $P(next), V(x\\_sem)$",
        "$V(next), P(x\\_sem)$ D. $P(x\\_sem), V(x\\_sem)$"
      ],
      "answer_from_source": "D",
      "code_blocks": [
        {
          "lang": "txt",
          "code": "P(mutex);\n...\nbody of procedure\n...\nif (next_count > 0)"
        },
        {
          "lang": "txt",
          "code": "V(next);\nelse\n    V(mutex);"
        },
        {
          "lang": "c",
          "code": "x_count = x_count + 1;\nif (next_count > 0)\n    V(next);\nelse\n    V(mutex);\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------- E1;\nx_count = x_count - 1;"
        },
        {
          "lang": "txt",
          "code": "if (x_count > 0)\n{\n    next_count = next_count + 1;\n    ----------------E2;\n    P(next);\n    next_count = next_count - 1;\n}"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume3.pdf",
        "volume": "filter1_volume3",
        "ref": "5.28.11",
