      "topic": "processes-threads",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "msq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2021,
      "text": "Consider the following multi-threaded code segment (in a mix of C and pseudo-code), invoked by two processes $P_{1}$ and $P_{2}$, and each of the processes spawns two threads $T_{1}$ and $T_{2}$: Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct?",
      "options": [
        "Both $P_{1}$ and $P_{2}$ will print the value of x as 2.",
        "At least of $P_{1}$ and $P_{2}$ will print the value of x as 4.",
        "At least one of the threads will print the value of y as 2.",
        "Both $T_{1}$ and $T_{2}$ , in both the processes, will print the value of y as 1."
      ],
      "answer": [
        0,
        3
      ],
      "code_blocks": [
        {
          "lang": "txt",
          "code": "int x = 0; // global\nLock L1; // global\nmain () {\n    create a thread to execute foo(); // Thread T1\n    create a thread to execute foo(); // Thread T2\n    wait for the two threads to finish execution;\n    print(x);}\nfoo() {\n    int y = 0;\n    Acquire L1;\n    x = x + 1;\n    y = y + 1;\n    Release L1;\n    print (y);}"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume3.pdf",
