      "text": "A system has a Translation Lookaside Buffer (TLB) that has a reach of 1 MB. TLB reach is defined as the total amount of physical memory that can be accessed through the TLB entries. The paging system uses pages of size 4 KB. The virtual address space is 64 GB and physical address space is 1 GB. If each TLB stores a 4-bit process id, page number, frame number, and a 2-bit control field, then the size of the TLB (in by \\_\\_\\_\\_. (answer in integer) Note: $1\\mathrm{K} = 2^{10}, 1\\mathrm{M} = 2^{20}, 1\\mathrm{G} = 2^{30}$",
