    {
      "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-5-33-35",
      "topic": "virtual-memory",
      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2019,
      "text": "Assume that in a certain computer, the virtual addresses are 64 bits long and the physical addresses are 48 bits long. The memory is word addressable. The page size is 8 kB and the word size is 4 bytes. The Translation Look-aside Buffer (TLB) in the address translation path has 128 valid entries. At most how many distinct virtual addresses can be translated without any TLB miss?",
      "options": [
        "$16 \\times 2^{10}$",
        "$256 \\times 2^{10}$",
        "$4 \\times 2^{20}$",
        "$8 \\times 2^{20}$"
      ],
