      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2008,
      "text": "A paging scheme uses a Translation Look-aside Buffer (TLB). A TLB-access takes 10 ns and the main memory access takes 50 ns. What is the effective access time(in ns) if the TLB hit ratio is 90% and there is no page-fault?",
      "options": [
        "54",
        "60",
        "65",
        "75"
      ],
      "answer": [
